# Logging

Every line helps someone diagnose a failure. No noise, no dumps.

## Rust (`tracing` only)

- No `println!`, `dbg!`, or `eprintln!`.
- Message is a fixed short phrase. Data goes in fields.
- One completion line per request: `request_id`, method, path, status, `latency_ms`. Also return `x-request-id`.
- `GET /healthz` is debug only. Other 2xx is info. 4xx is warn. 5xx is error.
- Log an error once, at the boundary that handles it. Include the cause chain. Do not log and also return the same error at every layer.
- Never log database URLs, tokens, request bodies, or provider prompts.
- No per-row logs. Summarize counts and duration.
- Pretty format when `APP_ENV` is not `production`. JSON in production. Level from `RUST_LOG`.

## Web

- Do not call `console` outside `apps/web/src/lib/logger.ts`.
- Production builds emit warn and error only.
- Log a failed API call once, inside `api-client`: method, path, status, `x-request-id`, duration. Never log payloads or tokens.
- Do not log renders, successful fetches, or navigation.
- Show a toast for a failure the user needs to see. The log is for developers.
